## 2026-09-09T19:05+02:00 — Pre-plan locked
- User locked the design after an /elegant pass. Committed path:
  1. Allocator: next = max(child_counters floor, highest existing immediate numeric child suffix) + 1, written back as the new floor. Counter kept deliberately as a monotonic floor (tombstones expire after 30 days, `bd delete` hard-deletes rows; reuse of a dead number would collide with git history or a peer). Never the source of truth.
  2. One storage operation `CreateChildIssue(ctx, parentID, issue, actor)`: inside one immediate transaction allocate-or-validate the ID, insert, record event, mark dirty, add the parent-child edge, commit. Replaces `GetNextChildID` in the Storage interface (removed; memory storage migrated too). CLI create and RPC create both call it and drop their own post-create parent-edge code.
  3. `insertIssue` / `insertIssues` become plain INSERT; UNIQUE-error suppression removed. Any final-ID collision rolls back before event, dirty mark, or edge.
  4. `--id` plus `--parent` allowed when the ID's immediate parent equals --parent; mismatch is an error before any write.
- Not in scope: counter key rename on prefix rename; making `--deps`/label failures fatal; farmplanner DB repair (handed to w893).
