+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| A1 | high | plan_v4.md:73,119; internal/storage/sqlite/multirepo.go:300; internal/storage/sqlite/store.go:206 | Multi-repo hydration, including the configured primary repository, inserts directly through `upsertIssueInTx` without either proposed insert helper, so hydrating `repro-p.1`, removing its row, and creating under `repro-p` can reissue `.1` because its floor was never raised. | Add hydration to the change list and raise each imported parent's maximum numeric child floor within its existing transaction after all rows have been inserted, with a hydration-then-deletion regression test. |
+| A2 | med | plan_v4.md:73,85,119 | The orphan guard discards the floor raise permanently when a child arrives before its parent in separate imports: importing `repro-p.1`, later importing `repro-p`, and removing the child before any allocation leaves neither a floor nor a child to scan, so the next create reissues `.1`. | When an absent parent is inserted, establish its floor from its existing immediate numeric children in that transaction, and test the orphan-first, parent-later, child-deleted ordering. |
+| A3 | med | plan_v4.md:161; internal/storage/sqlite/queries.go:867,992 | Prefix rename leaves the historical floor under the old parent ID, so a parent whose `.1` was created and purged can be renamed and allocate `.1` again, contradicting the stated reason that scanning repairs the lost floor. | Preserve parent floors across prefix rename and add a test that removes the highest child before renaming, since that child's number cannot be recovered by scanning surviving rows. |
+| A4 | med | plan_v4.md:57,117,119 | The unchecked `max(floor, maxExisting)+1` overflows for the accepted ID `repro-wide.9223372036854775807`, producing a negative suffix that `IsHierarchicalID` does not recognize, while floor maintenance has no stated policy for the also-accepted suffix `9223372036854775808`. | Define one numeric parsing policy for scans and floor writes that preserves acceptance of out-of-range explicit IDs by skipping their floor raise, reject allocation before incrementing the maximum representable value, and test both boundary inputs. |
+| A5 | med | plan_v4.md:126; internal/storage/sqlite/child_counters_test.go:127 | Rewriting the existing concurrency test against read-only `allocateChildNumber` retains an impossible guarantee, because ten calls without inserts all legitimately return the same next number rather than the ten distinct numbers asserted at lines 168–182. | Remove allocation-only uniqueness and progression expectations, test that repeated reads leave state unchanged, and keep uniqueness coverage solely on transactional `CreateChildIssue` calls. |
+| A6 | med | plan_v4.md:71,137; internal/importer/importer.go:350,470 | The proposed rename test with an already-existing identical target returns through the early recovery at lines 350–366 without reaching `CreateIssue`, so it cannot validate the newly live UNIQUE-error branch and the plan incorrectly describes this existing-target case as silent data loss. | Correct the existing-target description and make the recovery test deterministically create the identical target between the initial lookup and the attempted insert, for example through a test-only SQLite delete trigger, so it exercises the wrapped-error recovery at line 472. |
+| A7 | med | plan_v4.md:119,135,137 | None of the specified tests proves that batch insertion raises the maximum floor: allocation after import can succeed entirely through the scan, and the deletion test uses single-row explicit creation, so omitting batch floor maintenance or taking the last suffix instead of the maximum can pass the planned proof. | Add a batch test inserting children `.5` and `.3` in that order, assert floor 5, remove `.5`, and require the next child to be `.6`. |
+| A8 | med | plan_v4.md:315–319 | Gate 9 discards the test process's exit status and counts only lines beginning `FAIL`, which I reproduced reporting zero failures for `go test ./... -short` exiting 1 with `no packages to test` in a scratch repository. | Run gate 9 from an explicitly retained worktree root and require the actual `go test` exit status to be zero instead of inferring success from its output text. |

